==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|obvious|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɑ(b).vi(.)əs.li/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɒ(b).vi.əs.li/|q2=informal|/ˈɒ(b).vɪəs.li/|/ˈɒ(b).vjəs.li/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɔ(b).vi.ɘs.li/|q2=informal|/ˈɔv.jɘs.li/|a=NZ}}
* {{hyph|en|ob|vi|ous|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-obviously.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In an [[obvious]] or [[clearly]] [[apparent]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|She was in floods of tears and '''obviously''' very upset.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=8|passage=It was a casual sneer, '''obviously''' one of a long line. There was hatred behind it, but of a quiet, chronic type, nothing new or unduly virulent, and he was taken aback by the flicker of amazed incredulity that passed over the younger man's ravaged face.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{n-g|Used as a filler word, or to introduce information even when not obvious.}}
#: {{ux|en|You weren't to know, but I've spoken to, '''obviously''', Jim about this, and ...}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|in an obvious manner}} {{l|en|apparently}}, {{l|en|clearly}}, {{l|en|evidently}}, {{l|en|manifestly}}, {{l|en|obvi}}; see also [[Thesaurus:obviously]]

